    "deep-metro-1950s": {
      "name": "Deep metro (1950–1957)",
      "names": {"pl":"Metro głębokie (1950–1957)"},
      "status": "abandoned",
      "description": "A Y-shaped deep-level line decided in 1950, from Plac Komuny Paryskiej (Plac Wilsona) to Plac Unii Lubelskiej with a branch from ul. Próżna under the Vistula to Dworzec Wileński and a depot at Targówek. Work began on the Praga side in 1951, was cut back to a trial section in 1953 and stopped in 1957, leaving a 1.3 km tunnel near ul. Radzymińska.",
